course: dictionary
lesson: 7049
title: Passport: a book and a key
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A passport is an official book from your country's government. It has your photo, name and date of birth inside, and you show it when you travel to another country. «You cannot travel to another country without a passport, so keep it safe and with an adult.»
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. In «Bianca's family planned to leave for the airport at 9:00 but left at 9:25 because Mum lost her passport», the clues are the airport and leaving for a trip. So a passport must be something you need to travel.
explain: Passport also has a second meaning: something that helps you get or reach something. In «a passport to success», the word passport is not a book at all. It means something that helps you reach success. The sentence around it tells you which meaning fits.
fact: A passport is an official small book from your country's government.
fact: Your passport has your photo, name and date of birth in it.
fact: «Passport control» is the place at the airport where you show your passport before you travel abroad.
fact: Keep your passport safe, and never post photos of it online.
fact: «Inside most of the European Union, the Schengen Area lets people cross borders without passport checks.»
exercise: «Bianca's family left late because Mum lost her passport.» What is a passport? | A map of the airport | A small, clear bag for liquids | A ticket that lets you sit anywhere on the plane | *An official book from your country's government, with your photo and name
exercise: What does «passport control» mean? | Shop where you buy sweets | *Place at the airport where you show your passport to travel abroad | Seat on the plane | Bag for liquids at security
exercise: In «a passport to success», what does passport mean? | A book you take on holiday | A photo of yourself | *Something that helps you get or reach success | A rule about travel
test: Why must you keep your passport safe and with an adult? | Because it is heavy to carry | *Because you cannot travel abroad without it | Because it is good to read at night | Because it has pictures of food
test: Inside the Schengen Area, what does the text say about borders? | People must always queue for hours | Borders are closed to children | *People can cross borders without passport checks | Everyone must pay at every border
exam: Which phrase uses passport in its second meaning? | «a valid passport» | *«a passport to success» | «passport control» | «renew a passport»
